---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/config/site';
import { LIVE } from '@/data/jobs';
import { COMPANIES } from '@/data/companies';
import { ROUNDS } from '@/data/ecosystem';
import { ANCHORED_COUNTIES } from '@/data/counties';
const regionalAnchors = ANCHORED_COUNTIES.filter((c) => c.id !== 'nairobi');
const nairobiCount = COMPANIES.filter((c) => c.hq === 'Nairobi').length;
---
<Base title="Methodology — how startups.co.ke keeps data honest" description="Status tags, verification rules, sourcing standards, jobs board pipeline, salary disclosure policy and update cadence on startups.co.ke.">
  <article class="wrap max-w-3xl py-10">
    <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-mut"><a href="/" class="hover:text-ink">Home</a> / Methodology</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(32px,3.8vw,50px)]">How the data works.</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-mut">Compiled from public sources · as of Oct 16, 2026 · maintained by the desk</p>

    <div class="prose-sck mt-8">
      <p><strong>The one rule.</strong> Every figure on this platform carries a status and a named public source. If we can't source it, it doesn't go up — including numbers that would flatter the index. That rule is the product: a directory full of unsourced numbers is noise, and investors, journalists and founders all need numbers they can repeat.</p>

      <h2 id="statuses">Status tags</h2>
      <p><strong>Verified</strong> — a profile cross-checked against at least two independent public sources (press, registries, investor announcements). Unverified profiles are shown with a dashed tag until checks clear.</p>
      <p><strong>Confirmed</strong> — a round confirmed by a company statement or the lead investor's own memo.</p>
      <p><strong>Reported</strong> — credible secondary reporting, awaiting confirmation by the company or lead.</p>
      <p><strong>Estimated</strong> — modelled from registry filings, comparable deals or clearly-stated assumptions. Always shown with how it was derived.</p>
      <p><strong>Undisclosed</strong> — the amount was never made public. It renders as "Undisclosed", never as zero or $0K.</p>
      <p><strong>Failure states</strong> — administration, liquidation, shutdown and restructuring are tracked and displayed like funding states, with dates and sources. Tracked failures so far: 13, with Sh93bn in investor losses (Business Daily, Sep 2026).</p>

      <h2 id="rounds">Rounds feed</h2>
      <p>The <a class="text-amber underline" href="/funding">funding database</a> holds {ROUNDS.length} tracked rounds, each with amount, round, lead, status, source and a note when reporting conflicts (e.g. "EcoNews reports $42M"). Dates are shown as published; when a source gives only a year or no date at all, the entry says so instead of inventing precision. Annual market totals ($984M in 2025, $126M in H1 2026) come from named press houses and are labelled with the source wherever they appear.</p>

      <h2 id="jobs">Jobs board</h2>
      <p>Live rows are pulled at build time from employers' own hiring systems — Lever, Greenhouse, Workable, BambooHR and Ashby — never from third-party scrapers. Every rebuild re-fetches; the current snapshot was fetched <strong>{LIVE.fetchedAt}</strong>. Application links are checked on every pull and expired listings drop off automatically, so a 404 shouldn't survive more than one build. You always apply on the employer's own portal; we don't sit in the middle. No salary is ever invented for a live row. Where an employer hides pay, we attach a market band from published surveys and label it a band, not an offer — because most Kenyan employers don't publish pay (Fuzu calls this market "zero salary transparency"), and a board that pretends otherwise is lying by omission. Coverage benchmark: StartupJobs Kenya tracked 54 startup roles nationwide (Oct 2026); our board's live count and per-board status are shown openly on the <a class="text-amber underline" href="/jobs">jobs page</a> and refresh with every build.</p>

      <h2 id="counties">Counties and anchors</h2>
      <p>All 47 counties appear on the map as geography. "Anchors" are extra: a named ecosystem hub in that county, verified against a public source (qz.com, AfriLabs, UNDP county profiles, UNESCO DigiKen 2025). There are <strong>{ANCHORED_COUNTIES.length} anchored counties out of 47 — Nairobi plus {regionalAnchors.length} regional hubs</strong> ({regionalAnchors.map((c) => c.name).join(', ')}). Nairobi is counted as one of the {ANCHORED_COUNTIES.length}; the separate "regional anchors" figure always means the {regionalAnchors.length} outside Nairobi. Most tracked startups are Nairobi-based ({nairobiCount} of {COMPANIES.length}) — we show that honestly rather than dressing it up.</p>

      <h2 id="updates">Update cadence</h2>
      <p>Company profiles, rounds and investor data are re-checked by the desk continuously and re-dated in bulk each time — the "compiled" stamp on every page is the honest as-of date. The jobs board and its per-board statuses refresh on every site build (builds run whenever data changes, at least daily for the jobs snapshot). News and research follow the desk's reading of the week, published in <a class="text-amber underline" href="/news">The Wire</a> and the <a class="text-amber underline" href="/research">research library</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
      <p>Spotted an error? Use "Report data issue" on any profile, or email <a class="text-amber underline" href={`mailto:${SITE.contact.email}`}>{SITE.contact.email}</a>. Corrections are applied after a human checks the source — usually within two working days — and the entry's source line is updated to reflect the fix. We'd rather be corrected than confident.</p>

      <h2 id="seosubmit">For founders: what listing gets you</h2>
      <p>A claimed profile is a public page of your own — what you do, stage, team, open roles, logo — indexable by search engines, searchable by the investors who use the platform for deal flow. It's free, reviewed by a person, and you keep control: report an issue any time to update or remove. The "Listed on startups.co.ke" badge is available to every listed company.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 border border-ink bg-paper2 p-6">
      <p class="mono-label">Anything look off?</p>
      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <a class="btn btn-amber" href="/contact">Contact the desk</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/about">About the platform</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
